# kex: run-beam
# kexhq/kex#360: the SMALLEST repro from the issue. This alone crashed erlc
# with `{key_exists,{b_local,{b_literal,close},2}}` before running a single
# line — no call to `close`/`closed?` anywhere, just the two `using`s
# together. Deliberately excludes `Net.HTTP.Client`: adding it was an
# unreliable workaround (see net_socket_websocket_close_collision_beam.kex
# for the version with Client and real close/closed? calls), not a fix, and
# this spec exists specifically to keep covering the case where that
# workaround isn't in play.
using Net.Socket
using Net.HTTP.WebSocket

main do
  IO.printLine("compiled fine")
end
